s-examples-v10","line":41},{"title":"Configure rules to manage findings","target":"sem-configure-rules-manage-findings","line":181},{"title":"Grouping multiple findings as remediation tasks for easy processing using remediation task rules","target":"sem-grouping-multiple-findings-remediation-tasks-processing","line":182},{"title":"Access control lists \\(ACLs\\) for administration rules","target":"sem-acls-for-admin-rules","line":183},{"title":"Security Exposure Management Workspace","target":"sem-workspace-user-interface","line":184},{"title":"Vulnerabilities","target":"vulnerabilities","line":185},{"title":"Vulnerability Response remediation task rule examples","target":"vul-group-rules-examples-v10","line":186}],"metadata":{"title":"Configuring remediation task rules","description":"By configuring remediation task rules, you can automatically group findings based on filter conditions.Create remediation task rules to automatically group findings based on filter conditions. These rules automatically group findings as they’re imported or manually created. Use the filter to limit the findings grouped by this rule, such as selecting all findings with exploits.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/sem-configure-remediation-task-rules.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":3,"breadcrumb":["Configure rules to manage findings","Implement","Unified Security Exposure Management","Security Operations"],"tags":["#security-management","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/security-management/sem-configure-remediation-task-rules.md"},
